---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Progress from '../components/Progress.astro';
const sections = [
  { id: 'target', label: 'Target' }, { id: 'gaps', label: 'Gaps' }, { id: 'plan', label: 'Weekly plan' },
  { id: 'resume', label: 'Resume' }, { id: 'messages', label: 'Messages' }, { id: 'aws-gcp', label: 'AWS → GCP' },
  { id: 'interview', label: 'Interview' }, { id: 'stories', label: 'STAR stories' },
];
---
<Base title="Google Plan" description="Google Cloud Customer Engineer II: target, gaps, weekly plan, resume edits and interview prep." brand="google">
<Progress plan="google" sections={sections} />

<p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:24px">Step 1 · Google Cloud</p>
<h1>Cloud Architect: action plan</h1>
<p class="sub">Goal: a Google Customer Engineer II offer by March 2027. Sources: the resume, two Google mentor calls (Pavan, Diyasini) and live Google job postings.</p>

<div class="card next">
  <div class="eyebrow">Do this next</div>
  <p class="act">Make the 6 resume edits in section 4 (about 2 hours), then send the two mentor messages in section 5.</p>
</div>

<h2 id="target"><span class="num">1</span>Your target</h2>
<div class="row">
  <div class="box ok"><div class="k">Apply to</div><div class="v"><a href="https://www.google.com/about/careers/applications/jobs/results/142655373306667718-customer-engineer-ii-platform-east-google-cloud" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Customer Engineer II, Platform</a></div><div class="meta">Needs 6 yrs (you have ~7). Base $127K–$184K + bonus + stock.</div></div>
  <div class="box"><div class="k">Backup</div><div class="v"><a href="https://www.google.com/about/careers/applications/jobs/results/114624657943864006-application-modernization-engineer-professional-services-google-cloud" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Application Modernization Engineer, Prof. Services</a></div><div class="meta">Austin TX. Base $152K–$221K. Expect a coding round.</div></div>
  <div class="box no"><div class="k">Don't apply</div><div class="v">"Must be a US Citizen", clearance roles, CE III (needs 10 yrs)</div></div>
</div>
<p class="note">Why this role: it's Google's version of the AWS Solutions Architect. Its preferred skills (infrastructure modernization, migrations, security) are your strongest work. Both mentors confirmed AWS L5 maps to Google L4, which is the CE II level.</p>

<h2 id="gaps"><span class="num">2</span>The 3 gaps to close (nothing else)</h2>
<div class="tbl"><table>
<tr><th>Gap</th><th>Why it matters</th><th>How you close it</th></tr>
<tr><td>1. Google Cloud vocabulary</td><td>Interviews don't test GCP products, but you must translate your AWS answers fluently</td><td>Section 6 table + Professional Cloud Architect exam on Dec 19</td></tr>
<tr><td>2. Agentic AI</td><td>Both mentors said it's asked even for infrastructure roles</td><td>Build one agent demo (week 6–7) + learn the 5 answers in section 7</td></tr>
<tr><td>3. Resume reads like delivery, not pre-sales</td><td>Customer Engineer recruiters look for "technical win, workshops, PoCs, executives"</td><td>Section 4 edits</td></tr>
</table></div>

<h2 id="plan"><span class="num">3</span>Week-by-week plan <small>(~10 hrs/week: 1 hr on weekdays, 2.5 hrs each weekend day)</small></h2>

<div class="week"><h3>Week 1 · Oct 19–25 <span>Positioning</span></h3>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w1a"><label for="w1a">Make the 6 resume edits (section 4).<span class="done-when">Done when every bullet has a number and the words "customer", "workshop" or "PoC" appear at least 5 times.</span></label></div>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w1b"><label for="w1b">Send the referral heads-up to Pavan and Diyasini (section 5).<span class="done-when">Done when both messages are sent.</span></label></div>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w1c"><label for="w1c">Book the Google Professional Cloud Architect exam ($200) for Sat Dec 19 via cloud.google.com/learn/certification/cloud-architect.<span class="done-when">Done when you have the confirmation email.</span></label></div>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w1d"><label for="w1d">Create a Google Careers job alert: "Customer Engineer Platform", United States.<span class="done-when">Done when the alert is saved.</span></label></div>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w1e"><label for="w1e">In your Amazon stock portal and offer letter, write down your next RSU vest date and the sign-on bonus payback rule.<span class="done-when">Done when you know the cheapest month to resign.</span></label></div>
</div>

<div class="week"><h3>Week 2 · Oct 26 – Nov 1 <span>Stories</span></h3>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w2a"><label for="w2a">Write 8 STAR stories using the list in section 8. One paragraph each: Situation, Task, what <i>you</i> did, Result with a number.<span class="done-when">Done when you can tell each one aloud in under 2 minutes.</span></label></div>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w2b"><label for="w2b">Memorize the AWS → Google table (section 6).<span class="done-when">Done when you can say the Google name for all 15 rows without looking.</span></label></div>
</div>

<div class="week"><h3>Weeks 3–5 · Nov 2–22 <span>Learn Google Cloud</span></h3>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w3a"><label for="w3a">Complete the "Professional Cloud Architect" learning path on Google Cloud Skills Boost (cloudskillsboost.google), about 6 hrs a week.<span class="done-when">Done when all path modules are finished.</span></label></div>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w3b"><label for="w3b">Read the official PCA exam case studies (linked from the exam guide). For each one, draw the target architecture on paper.<span class="done-when">Done when every case study has a drawing. These double as practice for the presentation round.</span></label></div>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w3c"><label for="w3c">Practice 1 design question a week from section 7, timed at 35 min, drawing on paper.<span class="done-when">Done when you've done 3.</span></label></div>
</div>

<div class="week"><h3>Weeks 6–7 · Nov 23 – Dec 6 <span>Build one agent demo</span></h3>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w6a"><label for="w6a">Follow the Agent Development Kit (ADK) Python quickstart at google.github.io/adk-docs.<span class="done-when">Done when the sample agent runs locally.</span></label></div>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w6b"><label for="w6b">Build a "Migration Assistant" agent. Input: a CSV of 20 servers. Output: a migration approach per server (rehost, replatform or refactor) plus wave groups. Expose the CSV reader as an MCP tool.<span class="done-when">Done when it gives sensible output for your CSV.</span></label></div>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w6c"><label for="w6c">Deploy it to Cloud Run. Record a 3-minute screen video. Put the code on GitHub.<span class="done-when">Done when you have a public repo link and a video link to put on your resume.</span></label></div>
</div>

<div class="week"><h3>Weeks 8–9 · Dec 7–19 <span>Certify</span></h3>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w8a"><label for="w8a">Take the official PCA practice exam. Re-study weak areas and repeat until you score 85% or higher.<span class="done-when">Done when you score 85%+.</span></label></div>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w8b"><label for="w8b">Pass the exam on Dec 19. Add it to your resume and LinkedIn.<span class="done-when">Done when you pass.</span></label></div>
</div>

<div class="week"><h3>Weeks 10–11 · Dec 20 – Jan 3 <span>Rehearse</span></h3>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w10a"><label for="w10a">Build an 8-slide deck for the practice case in section 7 (presentation round). Present it aloud 3 times with a timer.<span class="done-when">Done when you can present it in 25 minutes.</span></label></div>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w10b"><label for="w10b">Do 2 mock interviews: one technical with a Google Customer Engineer (book on Topmate), one behavioral with a friend using section 7 questions.<span class="done-when">Done when both are finished and notes taken.</span></label></div>
</div>

<div class="week"><h3>Week 12 · Jan 4–10, 2027 <span>Apply</span></h3>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w12a"><label for="w12a">Send referral requests to Pavan and Diyasini with the exact job links (section 5).<span class="done-when">Done when the referrals are submitted.</span></label></div>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w12b"><label for="w12b">Apply to Customer Engineer II Platform + Application Modernization Engineer. Pick the newest posting IDs if these have closed (search the same title).<span class="done-when">Done when both applications are submitted.</span></label></div>
</div>

<div class="week"><h3>Jan – Mar 2027 <span>Interview</span></h3>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w13a"><label for="w13a">On the recruiter call, ask: "Which topics will the technical round cover, and is there a presentation round?"<span class="done-when">Done when you have the topics in writing.</span></label></div>
<div class="task"><input type="checkbox" id="w13b"><label for="w13b">Before accepting an offer, ask for a 20-minute chat with the hiring manager (Pavan's advice: the manager matters most).<span class="done-when">Done when the chat has happened.</span></label></div>
</div>

<h2 id="resume"><span class="num">4</span>Resume: 6 exact edits</h2>
<div class="tbl"><table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Change</th><th>Write this</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Fix the typo</td><td>"Compute Engineering" → "Computer Engineering". Add "(2022–2024)" after San Jose State.</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>Replace the summary</td><td>"Customer-facing cloud architect with 7+ years helping enterprise and public-sector customers migrate and modernize: mainframe and SAP migrations, landing zones, cost-optimized cloud platforms. Drives the technical win through discovery, PoCs and executive presentations, then leads delivery."</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>Replace the 8 "Key Highlights" with these 3</td><td>• Architected a State DMV mainframe modernization (400+ transactions, 500+ JCL jobs, 900+ RPCs).<br>• Cut customer cloud spend $600K/yr (ReachMobi) and $250K/yr (Tecfinics).<br>• Led SAP S/4HANA migration across 60+ sites; provisioning cut from 4 days to 3 hours.</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>Add a pre-sales line to Sapphire</td><td>"Technical lead in pre-sales and delivery; ran [N] customer discovery workshops and PoCs that launched 5 digital services in under 9 months." Use a real N.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>Add an executive line to AWS (only if true)</td><td>"Presented target-state architecture and migration roadmap to the [DMV CIO / steering committee]."</td></tr>
<tr><td>6</td><td>Add 2 skill lines; cut 1 bullet</td><td>Add "Cloud: AWS, Google Cloud, Azure" and (after week 7) "AI: Agent Development Kit, MCP, Vertex AI". Delete "securing $5K+ AWS credits".</td></tr>
</table></div>

<h2 id="messages"><span class="num">5</span>Messages to send</h2>
