Resume attached. Highlights: State DMV mainframe modernization, SAP across 60+ sites, $600K/yr cost savings. Thank you!</pre>

<h2 id="aws-gcp"><span class="num">6</span>AWS → Google translation (memorize)</h2>
<div class="tbl"><table>
<tr><th>AWS</th><th>Google Cloud</th><th>AWS</th><th>Google Cloud</th></tr>
<tr><td>Accounts / OUs / SCPs</td><td>Projects / Folders / Org Policy</td><td>S3</td><td>Cloud Storage</td></tr>
<tr><td>VPC (regional)</td><td>VPC (global), Shared VPC</td><td>RDS / Aurora</td><td>Cloud SQL / AlloyDB</td></tr>
<tr><td>Transit Gateway</td><td>Network Connectivity Center</td><td>DynamoDB</td><td>Firestore / Bigtable</td></tr>
<tr><td>Direct Connect</td><td>Cloud Interconnect</td><td>Redshift / Athena</td><td>BigQuery</td></tr>
<tr><td>EC2</td><td>Compute Engine</td><td>IAM roles</td><td>IAM + service accounts</td></tr>
<tr><td>EKS / Fargate / Lambda</td><td>GKE / Cloud Run / Cloud Run functions</td><td>Bedrock / SageMaker</td><td>Vertex AI</td></tr>
<tr><td>ALB / CloudFront</td><td>Cloud Load Balancing (one global IP) / Cloud CDN</td><td>CloudWatch</td><td>Cloud Monitoring / Logging</td></tr>
<tr><td>Migration Hub / MGN</td><td>Migration Center / Migrate to VMs</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
</table></div>

<h2 id="interview"><span class="num">7</span>Interview: rounds and the questions to prepare</h2>
<div class="tbl"><table>
<tr><th>Round</th><th>What it is</th><th>How to pass</th></tr>
<tr><td>Recruiter screen</td><td>30 min: fit, level, location</td><td>Say "L4, Customer Engineer II". Ask which topics the technical round covers.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Role-Related Knowledge (1–2 rounds)</td><td>Migration journeys, architecture design, cloud concepts. Not GCP-specific.</td><td>Ask clarifying questions → state assumptions → draw → explain trade-offs (cost vs reliability vs speed).</td></tr>
<tr><td>General Cognitive Ability</td><td>Hypothetical problems, not technical</td><td>Clarify → split into 3–4 areas → go deep on top 2 → recommend → say how you'd measure it.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Googleyness &amp; Leadership</td><td>Past behavior questions</td><td>STAR stories from section 8. Say "I", not "we".</td></tr>
<tr><td>Presentation</td><td>Present a solution to 3–4 people acting as the customer, then handle objections</td><td>Practice case below. Use the 8-slide structure.</td></tr>
</table></div>
<p class="sub">No coding for Customer Engineer roles (Diyasini). The Application Modernization role lists data structures and algorithms, so do 30 easy LeetCode problems in Python if you get that interview.</p>

<div class="card">
<b>Technical questions</b>
<div class="q"><b>Walk me through migrating a customer from on-prem to cloud. (★ mentor)</b><span>Discover (inventory, dependencies, cost) → Plan (business case, approach per app, waves) → Foundation (landing zone, network, IAM) → Migrate (pilot, then waves, cutover with rollback) → Optimize (rightsize, modernize). Give your SAP and DMV examples.</span></div>
<div class="q"><b>Design something like Instagram and scale it globally. (★ mentor)</b><span>Ask about scale first. Global load balancer + CDN → stateless services → object storage for media → database (Spanner if global) → cache → async queue for processing. Then cover failure and cost.</span></div>
<div class="q"><b>The customer wants to host in China, but there's no cloud region. (★ mentor)</b><span>Ask about legal rules first. Use a local partner cloud inside China, a control plane in Hong Kong or Singapore, and comply with licensing and data-export rules.</span></div>
<div class="q"><b>How do you modernize a mainframe?</b><span>Options: rehost, automated refactor, rewrite, retire. Cover data (DB2 → PostgreSQL), batch jobs, and parallel-run testing. Then your DMV numbers.</span></div>
<div class="q"><b>Design disaster recovery for 4-hour RTO / 1-hour RPO. Now make it 15 minutes.</b><span>Backup-restore → pilot light → warm standby → active-active. Each step costs more. Use your Medicaid and SAP numbers.</span></div>
<div class="q"><b>Which database would you choose, and why?</b><span>Cloud SQL (standard relational), AlloyDB (high-performance Postgres), Spanner (global and consistent), Bigtable (huge throughput), Firestore (documents).</span></div>
<div class="q"><b>The cloud bill rose 40%. What do you do?</b><span>Find the top services by cost, rightsize, commit discounts, Spot for batch, storage tiers, labels and budgets. Then your $600K story.</span></div>
</div>
<div class="card">
<b>Agentic AI (★ both mentors)</b>
<div class="q"><b>Why MCP instead of a normal API?</b><span>MCP is a standard protocol (JSON-RPC) that lets any agent discover and call tools with a schema. A REST API needs custom code for each app. MCP wraps APIs; it doesn't replace them.</span></div>
<div class="q"><b>What is A2A?</b><span>A protocol for agents talking to other agents. MCP is agent-to-tool; A2A is agent-to-agent.</span></div>
<div class="q"><b>How do you take an agent to production?</b><span>Develop (ADK + tools) → deploy (Cloud Run or Vertex AI Agent Engine) → scale (quotas, caching, small vs large model routing) → govern (least-privilege tools, human approval for risky actions, logging).</span></div>
<div class="q"><b>How do you evaluate an agent?</b><span>A test set of tasks. Measure success rate, correct tool calls, latency and cost. Re-run on every change.</span></div>
<div class="q"><b>System 1 vs System 2 models?</b><span>Fast single-pass models vs slower reasoning models. Route easy requests to fast ones, hard ones to reasoning ones.</span></div>
</div>
<div class="card">
<b>General Cognitive Ability</b>
<div class="q"><b>A dashboard was built for sales, but nobody uses it. Drive adoption. (★ asked per Diyasini)</b><span>Ask who it's for and what decision it supports → interview 5 users to find why → co-design fixes with 2 champions → put it where they already work → have leaders use it weekly → track weekly active users.</span></div>
<div class="q"><b>Three customers want a PoC this week and you can do one.</b><span>Rank by deal value, chance to win, urgency and reuse. Offer the other two alternatives. Agree the call with your sales lead.</span></div>
</div>
<div class="card">
<b>Presentation practice case</b>
<p style="margin:6px 0">"A state agency runs a 30-year-old mainframe for licensing (300 requests/second peak). Modernize within 24 months, keep personal data in-state, cut costs 30%."</p>
<p style="margin:6px 0"><b>8 slides:</b> customer goals → assumptions → current pain → target architecture → migration phases → cost and value → risks → next steps (PoC scope and success criteria).</p>
<p style="margin:6px 0"><b>Expect these objections:</b> too expensive (show 3-year cost), security (encryption, data perimeter, compliance), lock-in (containers, Terraform), no skills (training, partners), too slow (phased waves).</p>
</div>

